Rāma rejects retinue and asks bark garments --- Rāma asks spade and basket for fourteen years --- Kaikēyī herself brings bark clothes shamelessly --- Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa don sage garments --- Sītā trembles and cannot tie bark garment --- Rāma ties bark over Sītā silk himself --- Crowd cries shame on Daśaratha --- Daśaratha protests Sītā wearing kuśa bark --- Rāma commends grieving Kausalyā to father
